The main observation of their algorithm is that E(g2, d1, g1) = Σ (from i=1 to b_g1) [freq[i] * log2(d1 / g1)] - This represents the expected error for group g2 when computing frequency estimation under equal group-wise approximation factor.

The parent is discussing a method of fairness in data streaming, specifically focusing on frequency estimation with an equal group-wise approximation factor. The algorithm they're describing calculates the value of g1 that minimizes the difference between two sides of Equation (5). They mention that this equation may not hold for some integer values of g1 and aim to find the closest possible solution.

